From: dnf-for-termux <dev@termux.dev>
Date: Thu, 06 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Trigger auto gpgkey import on librepo "Bad GPG signature"

Termux's librepo, when the gpg keyring is empty, reports signature
verification failures with the generic "Bad GPG signature" message
(LRE_BADGPG in gpg_gpgme.c) instead of upstream's "Signing key not
found". The auto-import of the repo gpgkey (RepoPgp::import_key())
is gated on that upstream message, so repo_gpgcheck=1 fails whenever
the keyring is empty. Broaden the check so the import also triggers
when the error message mentions a "Bad GPG signature".

diff --git a/libdnf5/repo/repo_sack.cpp b/libdnf5/repo/repo_sack.cpp
--- a/libdnf5/repo/repo_sack.cpp
+++ b/libdnf5/repo/repo_sack.cpp
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@
         exception = rd_err;
         if (report_key_err) {
             std::string msg = rd_err.what();
-            if (msg.ends_with("Signing key not found")) {
+            if (msg.ends_with("Signing key not found") || msg.find("Bad GPG signature") != std::string::npos) {
                 return true;
             }
         }
